Article 45: The public security organ traffic management department receiving a cooperation investigation notice shall immediately arrange for interception or investigation. If a traffic accident fleeing vehicle or suspected vehicle is discovered, it shall be detained, the traffic accident fleeing person or a suspect matching the cooperation investigation notice shall be summoned according to law, and the relevant situation shall be promptly notified to the public security organ traffic management department at the place where the case occurred. The public security organ traffic management department at the place where the case occurred shall immediately dispatch traffic police to handle the transfer.
Article 46: After the public security organ traffic management department discovers a traffic accident fleeing vehicle or a traffic accident fleeing suspect, it shall revoke the cooperation investigation notice within the original scope and revoke the control through the national motor vehicle investigation and control system.
Article 47: During the investigation and handling of traffic accident fleeing cases by the public security organ traffic management department, if the victims of traffic accident fleeing cases and their family members inquire about the case investigation status with the public security organ traffic management department, except for content that shall not be made public according to law, the public security organ traffic management department shall inform them and make records.
Article 48: If the road traffic accident social assistance fund management institution has advanced rescue expenses or funeral expenses for the victim, the public security organ traffic management department shall, after the traffic accident fleeing case is solved, promptly notify the road traffic accident social assistance fund management institution in writing of the relevant situation of the traffic accident fleeing driver.
Section 4: Inspection and Appraisal
Article 49: Where inspection or appraisal is required, the public security organ traffic management department shall, in accordance with relevant regulations, entrust a qualified appraisal institution to conduct inspection or appraisal within three days from the date the accident scene investigation is concluded.
Corpse inspection shall be entrusted within three days from the date of death. Inspection and appraisal of traffic accident fleeing vehicles shall be entrusted within three days from the date the suspected offending vehicle is discovered.
Where inspection or appraisal is required after three days from the conclusion of the scene investigation, approval shall be obtained from the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level.
Appraisal of mental illness shall be conducted by an appraisal institution with qualifications for mental illness appraisal.
Article 50: Inspection and appraisal fees shall be borne by the public security organ traffic management department, except as otherwise provided by laws and regulations or where the parties entrust disability assessment or property loss assessment on their own.
Article 51: The public security organ traffic management department shall determine the time limit for completion of inspection and appraisal with the appraisal institution, and the determined time limit shall not exceed thirty days. If it exceeds thirty days, approval shall be obtained from the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level, but the maximum shall not exceed sixty days.
Article 52: Corpse inspection shall not be conducted in public places. Where it is necessary to dissect a corpse to determine the cause of death, the consent of the deceased's family members shall be obtained. If the deceased's family members disagree to dissect the corpse, upon approval by the person in charge of a public security organ at or above the county level or the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level, the corpse may be dissected, and the deceased's family members shall be notified to be present and sign on the corpse dissection notice.
If the deceased's family members refuse to be present or refuse to sign without justifiable reasons, the traffic police shall note it on the corpse dissection notice. For corpses of unknown identity where the deceased's family members cannot be notified, it shall be recorded on file.
Article 53: After the corpse inspection report is determined, the deceased's family members shall be notified in writing to handle funeral matters within ten days. If they fail to handle it within the time limit without justifiable reasons, it shall be recorded on file, and upon approval by the person in charge of a public security organ at or above the county level or the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level, the public security organ or the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level shall handle the corpse, and the expenses for overdue storage shall be borne by the deceased's family members.
For those without family members, with unknown family members, or where notification is impossible or family members refuse to claim the body after notification due to force majeure such as natural disasters, upon approval by the person in charge of a public security organ at or above the county level or the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level, the body may be handled in a timely manner.
For corpses of unknown identity, after the forensic doctor extracts personal identification samples, photographs the corpse, and collects relevant information, the public security organ traffic management department shall fill out the information registration form for corpses of unknown identity and publish a notice for claiming the body in a newspaper at or above the municipal level where the city is divided into districts. If no one claims the body within thirty days after publication, upon approval by the person in charge of a public security organ at or above the county level or the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level, the body may be handled in a timely manner.
Where there are special needs for the time limit for handling corpses due to religious customs or other reasons, upon approval by the person in charge of a public security organ at or above the county level or the public security organ traffic management department at the next higher level, the body may be handled urgently.
Article 54: The appraisal institution shall complete the inspection and appraisal within the prescribed time limit and issue a written inspection report and appraisal opinion, signed by the appraiser, and the appraisal opinion shall also be affixed with the institution's seal. The inspection report and appraisal opinion shall state the following matters:
(1) The client;
(2) The date and matters of entrustment;
(3) The relevant materials submitted;
(4) The time of inspection and appraisal;
(5) The basis and conclusive opinion; where a conclusive opinion is drawn through analysis, there shall be an analysis proving process.
The inspection report and appraisal opinion shall be attached with qualification certificates or other supporting documents of the appraisal institution and appraisers.
Article 55: The public security organ traffic management department shall review the inspection report and appraisal opinion, and within five days from the date of receiving the inspection report and appraisal opinion, deliver copies of the inspection report and appraisal opinion to the parties, except in any of the following circumstances:
(1) The inspection or appraisal procedure is illegal or violates relevant professional technical requirements, which may affect the fairness and objectivity of the inspection report and appraisal opinion;
(2) The appraisal institution or appraiser does not possess appraisal qualifications and conditions;
(3) The inspection report and appraisal opinion are obviously insufficient in basis;
(4) A false appraisal is intentionally made;
(5) The appraiser should have recused himself/herself but did not;
