The public security organ traffic management department shall, within ten days from the date mediation commences, prepare a Road Traffic Accident Damage Compensation Mediation Agreement or a Road Traffic Accident Damage Compensation Mediation Termination Document.
Article 91 Traffic police mediating road traffic accident damage compensation shall implement the following procedures:
(1) Informing all parties of their rights and obligations;
(2) Listening to the requests and reasons of all parties;
(3) Determining the damage compensation liability to be borne by the parties based on the facts determined in the Road Traffic Accident Determination and the provisions of Article 76 of the Road Traffic Safety Law of the People's Republic of China;
(4) Calculating the amount of damage compensation, determining the proportion to be borne by each party; the standards for personal injury compensation shall be implemented in accordance with relevant provisions such as the Tort Liability Law of the People's Republic of China, the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Application of Law in the Trial of Personal Injury Compensation Cases, and the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Application of Law in the Trial of Road Traffic Accident Damage Compensation Cases; the repair costs and depreciation compensation costs for property loss shall be calculated based on the actual value or the assessment conclusion of an appraisal agency;
(5) Determining the method and time limit for the performance of compensation.
Article 92 Where it is necessary to conduct disability assessment or property loss assessment to determine the amount of damage compensation, the parties shall jointly determine a qualified agency to conduct it; however, where the amount of property loss is huge and involves suspicion of a criminal offense, it shall be entrusted by the public security organ traffic management department.
The costs of disability assessment and property loss assessment entrusted by the parties shall be borne by the parties.
Article 93 Where an agreement is reached through mediation, the public security organ traffic management department shall prepare a Road Traffic Accident Damage Compensation Mediation Agreement on the spot, which shall be signed by all parties and served to each party respectively.
The mediation agreement shall state the following:
(1) The basis for mediation;
(2) The basic facts and loss situation determined in the Road Traffic Accident Determination;
(3) The items and amounts of damage compensation;
(4) The damage compensation liability and proportion of each party;
(5) The method and time limit for the performance of compensation;
(6) The date of mediation.
Where the parties fail to reach an agreement through mediation, the public security organ traffic management department shall terminate the mediation, prepare a Road Traffic Accident Damage Compensation Mediation Termination Document, and serve it to each party.
Article 94 Under any of the following circumstances, the public security organ traffic management department shall terminate the mediation and record it:
(1) One party files a civil lawsuit with the people's court during the mediation period;
(2) One party fails to participate in mediation without justifiable reason;
(3) One party withdraws from mediation during the mediation process.
Article 95 Public security organ traffic management departments in places with conditions may, in conjunction with relevant departments, establish road traffic accident insurance claim service venues.
Chapter 10  Handling of Road Traffic Accidents Involving Foreigners
Article 96 Where a foreigner has a road traffic accident within the territory of the People's Republic of China, in addition to complying with these provisions, they shall also comply with the provisions of relevant laws, regulations, and rules concerning the handling of foreign-related cases.
The public security organ traffic management department handling road traffic accidents involving foreigners shall inform the parties of their rights and obligations in handling road traffic accidents as prescribed by Chinese laws, regulations, and rules.
Article 97 A foreigner who has a road traffic accident under any of the following circumstances shall not be allowed to exit the country:
(1) Suspected of a crime;
(2) There is an unsettled road traffic accident damage compensation case, and the people's court has decided not to allow exit;
(3) Other circumstances where exit is not permitted as prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.
Article 98 Where a foreigner has a road traffic accident and bears full or main responsibility, the public security organ traffic management department shall inform the right holder of road traffic accident damage compensation that they may request the people's court to take pre-litigation preservation measures.
Article 99 The public security organ traffic management department shall use the commonly used spoken and written language of the People's Republic of China in handling road traffic accidents. For those who do not understand the language and written characters of our country, translation shall be provided; where a party understands the language and written characters of our country and does not need translation by others, they shall issue a written statement.
Upon approval by the public security organ traffic management department, a foreigner may hire a translator on their own, and the translation costs shall be borne by the party.
Article 100 When a person enjoying diplomatic privileges and immunities has a road traffic accident, they shall actively present valid identity documents. Where traffic police consider that the motor vehicle driver's license should be temporarily detained or revoked, they may detain the motor vehicle driver's license. Where it is necessary to investigate a person enjoying diplomatic privileges and immunities, they may be interviewed, and the conversation shall be limited to content related to the road traffic accident. Where it is necessary to inspect or appraise the vehicle, the public security organ traffic management department shall obtain their consent and return it immediately after inspection or appraisal.
The public security organ traffic management department shall prepare a Road Traffic Accident Determination based on the collected evidence and serve it to the party; if the party refuses to accept it, it shall be served to their institution; if there is no institution or the institution is unclear, it shall be transferred for service through the embassy or consulate of the country to which the party belongs in China.
A person enjoying diplomatic privileges and immunities shall cooperate with the investigation and inspection or appraisal by the public security organ traffic management department. For those who are verified to indeed enjoy diplomatic privileges and immunities but do not agree to accept investigation or inspection or appraisal, the public security organ traffic management department shall record the relevant circumstances, and damage compensation matters shall be resolved through diplomatic channels.
